# The scheduler is a POSIX shell script and a crontab. Both are executed by
# /bin/sh on a Linux host, where a stray carriage return is not whitespace: it
# becomes part of the command name, and the job dies with "\r: not found" on
# every run -- after it was installed, scheduled, and reported as working.
#
# Git's autocrlf applies on checkout, so on a Windows contributor's machine
# these files would silently acquire CRLF. Pinning the line endings here makes
# the working tree correct regardless of each developer's core.autocrlf, and
# keeps the shebang and the cron command intact.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.cron text eol=lf
deploy/scheduler/** text eol=lf
